# REPEATABILITY. A and B are the same measurement of the same two curves and
# they differ: forward 137.5 against 145.5, back -152.9 against -147.3, about
# 8mm apart. Pass C below widens that to about 14mm and is the figure to quote.
# Either way the prose says "about 145mm" (the three-pass mean is 144.7mm
# forward, 146.0mm back) rather than carrying a tenth of a millimetre that
# does not survive another run. The SIGN is what carries the
# argument and it is identical in every pass and in the offline probe
# (pitch-0909.log: -121.8mm on this family, +136.1mm on the two 1.0 bodies).
#
# WHICH WAY IS FORWARD, read off the camera rather than inferred from another
# gesture. avatarGuideEngine sets camera.position.set(0, y + AVATAR_CAMERA_TILT,
# framingDistance) and AVATAR_FRAMING_DEFAULT.distance is 2.3, so the camera is
# at positive Z and +Z is toward the viewer. VRMUtils.rotateVRM0 sets
# scene.rotation.y = Math.PI on a 0.x body, turning a model that faces -Z round
# to face it.
#
# The nod row above is NOT that anchor, though an earlier draft used it as one.
# nod's pitch peaks at 0.14 rad and is 0.078 at the 720ms sample, worth about
# 4.5mm of eye swing against the 10.9mm recorded: it sits inside the same band as
# the eight gestures this file calls unchanged. It stays in the table as one more
# reading, not as evidence.
#
# THE OTHER EIGHT. Pass B clicked every gesture the preview offers. None moved
# beyond the idle floor except `glance`, at +92.9mm, which is a head turn and is
# supposed to. Nothing else changed when `bow` did.
#
== pass C, 11:56, the screenshots, each bound to the frame it was read on ==
  gesture     peak    at      ink    baseline eye Z
  bow      +151.1mm   720ms   0.185   +0.0252m
  leanBack -137.8mm   728ms   0.182   +0.0107m
#
# THE FIRST PAIR OF SCREENSHOTS DID NOT SHOW THESE POSES, and both reviewers
# caught it independently. The two PNGs committed at 10:56 were two near-idle
# frames: 172,428 against 172,427 foreground pixels, silhouette centroid 0.6px
# apart, mask XOR 6,201px, the whole difference a 4px sideways shift that is the
# idle weight shift. A capture taken by an outside screenshot tool cannot be
# aimed at a 1.5s envelope, because its latency is not bounded by anything.
#
# Pass C aims it from inside the page instead, and the reading and the pixels
# come from ONE frame:
#
#   * every frame after the click, record elapsed time and the eye's Z;
#   * on the first frame at or past 715ms, read Z, then read the canvas;
#   * afterwards, confirm that frame was the largest |Z| of the whole trace.
#     It was, for both: 720ms and 728ms are the argmax, not a nominal 720.
#
# `ink` is the fraction of a downsampled copy of the canvas that is not black,
# taken in the same frame. It guards the one way this capture fails silently:
# the renderer runs with preserveDrawingBuffer false, so reading the canvas on
# the wrong side of a paint returns a blank image. 0.185 and 0.182 are the
# character; a cleared buffer reads 0.
#
# Playwright drove this pass, not the extension that drove A and B, because the
# extension was not connected. Its rAF is not starved here: 61 callbacks in a
# measured second on this page. The engine, body and camera are the same.
#
# The pair now differ as two poses. Foreground is a pixel whose RGB differs
# from the corner background by more than 12 on the channel mean:
#
#   foreground pixels      571,922 against 561,288
#   topmost foreground row      40 against 49, so 9px apart
#   foreground centroid, Y  605.91 against 672.47, so 66.6px apart
#   mask XOR                                       173,102px
#
# An earlier draft said the top edge was 16px apart. That figure came from
# "the first row holding more than 20 foreground pixels", a caliper picked
# after the fact and never written down. The topmost row is 9px.
# Both are cropped from the 2140x1456 canvas with ONE shared box (518,393)-
# (1651,1456), so they stay comparable to each other.
#
# Screenshots: bow-0910-bow.png, bow-0910-leanback.png.
#
# Three passes now, so the spread is 137.5/145.5/151.1 forward and
# 152.9/147.3/137.8 back: about 14mm, wider than the 8mm two passes suggested.
# The idle baseline itself moved 14.5mm between the two pass C runs, which is
# that same floor. The SIGN is what carries the argument and it is the same in
# all three passes, in the offline probe, and in the two screenshots.
